it's time to play another game  the saw series is coming back from the  dead with spiral  from the book of saw and this time there  are no rules  if you want to learn more about what to  expect from spiral  well you've come to the right place  you want to play games  the first saw film shocked audiences  back in october 2004  setting the tone for the torturous form  of horror that dominated the genre  during that decade  from 2004 up until 2010 horror fans got  a new saw film  every year as a halloween present with  jigsaw  the eighth installment in the franchise  hitting theaters in 2017.  now we'll get to see what the next  chapter in the book of saw  spiral has in store that spiral is what  i think it is  jigsaw wait i thought the jigsaw killer  was dead yeah but if it's another  copycat  it's going to be it's been a long  journey for the ninth film in the saw  franchise  originally the movie was set for release  in october 2020  but it looks like another senior horror  franchise elbowed its way  back into that territory after the  success of 2018's halloween  michael myers was supposed to return for  everybody's favorite spooky holiday  with follow-up halloween kills which was  originally planned for a 2020 release  most likely not wanting to compete with  the man in the william shatner mask  spiral changed its release date to may  15  2020. of course as we all know  neither horror film made it to theaters  as intended  as the world was turned upside down and  theaters closed by the covet 19 pandemic  however you can't stop a good slasher  franchise from coming back to life  and now spiral from the book of saw is  set to hit theaters and  imax on may 14th 2021  the cast of spiral from the book of saw  sounds pretty impressive  especially for something so outlandish  as a saw movie  first up we've got chris rock whether  you know him from his stand up  his more comedic acting work or his  serious dramatic roles  we can all agree that rock is a  charismatic and thoughtful performer  so it will be super fascinating to see  him take the lead  in a horror franchise as messed up as  the saw series  in fact in a refreshing twist rock  happens to be  one of the major creative forces behind  the film his pitch for the movie  is reportedly responsible for it  existing in the first place  but more on that later in spiral rock  plays  detective zeke banks a cop who's  investigating a new string of gruesome  murders  with some familiar iconography of course  he isn't handling the case alone  rock will be accompanied by max mingela  who will be playing  zeke's rookie partner if you think  mingela looks familiar  that's probably because you've seen him  as nick in the handmaid's tale  both detectives are working for captain  angie garza  played by marisol nichols of riverdale  and 24  fame of course the biggest name involved  is samuel l  jackson the man who brought nick fury  mace windu  and jules winfield to life will be  playing police veteran  marcus banks the accomplished but  estranged father of chris rock's  character  his casting adds a serious hook to a  film some people might otherwise write  off  a ninth saw movie well maybe you feel  like you've seen it before  a saw movie with samuel l jackson though  that's all you had to say  here's where things get really  interesting with this new saw film  the seed for the story came from an  unlikely person  chris rock variety reports that rock  approached some of the producers behind  the saw franchise with his idea for a  new film  and spiral from the book of saw grew  from that concept  joe drake chairman of lionsgate motion  picture group  set of rock's treatment when chris rock  came to us and described in chilling  detail his fantastic vision that  reimagines  and spins off the world of the notorious  jigsaw killer  we were all in honestly we are too  rock wrote the original story for spiral  but he didn't write the film's final  screenplay  pete goldfinger and josh stolberg who  also wrote 2017's jigsaw  adapted rock's story into spiral  screenplay the duo also wrote the  surprisingly fun remake of piranha  in 2010 the saw films vary in quality  and a big part of that is due to how  quickly they were being put together  one film every year is a hectic pace one  aspect that many fans still agree on  however  is that the saw films were in good hands  when director  darren lynn bausman was at the helm he  directed saw 2  saw 3 and saw 4 helping play off the  momentum of the original  and makes saw a household name and now  bausman is back in the director's chair  for spiral  from the book of saw bausman himself  announced that he'd be directing the  film on his instagram  posting an on-set photo from the first  day of production in july 2019  meanwhile long time franchise heads mark  berg  and oren kulas are also involved as  producers  even better still james wan and lee  wannell  the original duo who brought jigsaw to  life and have since given us  modern horror classics like the  conjuring and the invisible man  are serving as executive producers so if  anything is going to help bring the saw  franchise back from the dead  it's this team so how exactly  does spiral from the book of saw fit  into the timeline of the franchise  is it a sequel is it a total reboot well  for answers we can look to the twitter  account of josh stolberg one of the  writers for the film  in 2019 he responded to a curious fan  saying of the new movie it's not a  sequel to jigsaw  it's definitely in the timeline of all  the films though  with that out of the way what's the plot  of this new film  as it turns out spiral is set years  after jigsaw's death but his memory  still  looms large over the world in fact it  seems that he's inspired a copycat  killer one who's targeting cops into  this bloody game  comes chris zeke banks he's a detective  who's been saddled with a rookie partner  and according to the official plot  synopsis is working in the shadow of his  father  you pull a gun on your own man  yeah i could have killed you what are  you talking about i got the gun  i could have killed you but as the  bodies start piling up  zeke is forced to reunite with his  estranged dad to solve this case  and figure out the copycat's motive  which might involve  a twisted form of justice horror and  humor  have a lot in common both relying on  good timing  atmosphere and the right build up of  tension and release  horror has always been closely tied with  humor whether a film is providing  respite from blood and gore  lulling the audience into a false sense  of security or just playing with the  stereotypes of the genre  a good joke can go a long way when it  comes to lightening the mood of an  otherwise  dark movie chris rock isn't always  trying to be funny  but you still might think that his  involvement in spiral from the book of  saw  could make for a movie that's a bit  lighter in tone than the rest of this  relentlessly bleak series but it seems  like that isn't entirely the case  speaking with ign rock said that spyral  will have some humorous  elements mainly because the franchise  was completely lacking them  he said i love saw but i was like wow it  has almost no humor  at all so it seemed like a good place  good fertile ground  saying that he'd already seen a rough  cut of the movie he reported  it's still saw it's bloody it's gory but  there's like a sprinkling of humor here  and there we're not revamping it  it's not scary movie it's saw of course  he wants us to cut through our feet  you go first every horror franchise  has its big bad the friday the 13th  movies have jason  the nightmare on elm street movies have  freddy krueger  and the saw series has john cramer aka  the jigsaw killer granted he died back  in the third film  but his legacy still haunts the  franchise as his apprentices keep  popping up to  play nasty games with unwilling  participants  but will jon kramer appear in spiral  from the book of saw  well maybe in one of the trailers we see  a stack of photos and if you're paying  close attention  you'll notice that one of them is jigsaw  himself so at the very least  we'll see a very literal snapshot of the  man but will actor tobin bell  actually reappear somehow well in a  collider interview back in october 2020  bell was asked if he was psyched for the  film and if he would reprise his iconic  role  his answer oh yeah i'm excited for it  but it's not something i can really talk  about at this particular moment  well that's an interesting answer indeed  based on that response alone  it seems belle very well might be  involved with spiral  granted the movie isn't listed on bell's  imdb  page and he hasn't shown up in any of  the promotional materials aside from  that one  old photograph most importantly his  character is dead  but when does that stop the slasher  villain from coming back  after all cramer showed up in 2017's  jigsaw via flashbacks  so maybe bell will return for one last  game  at the very least john cramer's  influence will be  all over this film as his copycat starts  a new reign of terror  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite horror movies are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

